	// Fetches, now, the documents the tenant's accredited e-invoicing provider holds for the companies of
	// an `einvoice_provider` connector (ADR-0061 §4, T65a; SAP Document and Reporting Compliance's
	// inbound e-documents): the fetch is queued as an Operation (kind `einvoicing.fetch`), the request
	// audited in the caller's name (`einvoicing.fetch.request`, the Operation its object, with the
	// connector), and carried out as the workflow `FetchEInvoices`, or in process in a cell without a
	// workflow engine, as a system principal acting for the connector's companies. It lists the documents
	// the provider has not had acknowledged, and records each once per connector and the provider's
	// message id: its bytes kept write-once in object storage under their SHA-256, the document `received`
	// with its company (the connector's company whose participant identifier the provider listed it for;
	// none when it names none of them), the fetch's Operation as its `fetch_operation_id`, an audit record
	// and EInvoiceChanged; after that commit the provider is told the document is kept (its
	// acknowledgement), and `acknowledged_at` is set. A document already recorded is not recorded again
	// and its acknowledgement is sent again, so an acknowledgement lost is repaired by the next fetch. A
	// message delivered again under its id with other bytes (T65b) is not recorded again either: the
	// document keeps its first bytes, the legal original, and records the new bytes' SHA-256 as
	// `changed_sha256` with `changed_at`, with an audit record and EInvoiceChanged once per different
	// bytes, so the same changed bytes delivered again change nothing more. Its acknowledgement moves the
	// document's version without an event. Then the fetch processes every document of the connector not
	// processed yet, oldest first (T65c, ADR-0061 §5): it reads it as PINT AE (no DTD, no entity
	// expanded) and refuses it, `refused` with its `problem_code` and `problem_detail`, an audit record
	// and EInvoiceChanged, when it is unreadable, not a tax invoice 380 or tax credit note 381 following
	// PINT AE, lacks a field the ERP reads, states an amount with more decimals than its currency has,
	// does not add up without any tax rule, or is not addressed to the company (its buyer's electronic
	// address IBT-049 the company's participant, its buyer's TRN IBT-048 the company's FTA registration on
	// its issue date); a valid one stays `received`, with what was read (number, kind, issue date,
	// currency, gross, specification) and the release validated against, and a valid tax invoice is then
	// entered (T65d, ADR-0061 §6) as a supplier invoice of source `einvoice` by capture's rules without a
	// model: the purchase order its order reference (IBT-013) names, whose supplier must hold the seller's
	// TRN (IBT-031) as a tax identifier; its items by order line (IBT-132) or by position, each with its
	// order item's unit and tax code where that code has the line's VAT category (IBT-151) and charges its
	// rate (IBT-152), else the one input code that does, else the invoice on hold for a person to choose;
	// parked, or on hold with capture's reasons; its document the e-invoice's bytes
	// (`getSupplierInvoiceDocument`), published as SupplierInvoiceCaptured. The document becomes
	// `entered`, naming the invoice, with an audit record and EInvoiceChanged. Any refusal of the entering
	// (no order: `payables.capture_needs_order`; an unknown order or item, the seller's TRN not the
	// supplier's `payables.einvoice_seller_unknown`, `payables.duplicate_invoice`,
	// `payables.already_captured`, a closed period and any other) holds the document instead, `held` with
	// that problem's code and detail, nothing of the entering kept; a tax invoice or tax credit note not
	// in AED is entered keeping its VAT in AED as it states it, the sum of its lines' VAT in AED
	// (BTAE-08), as the invoice's `stated_local_tax`, which its posting keeps as the tax's local amount
	// (ADR-0061 As built batch 88), and is held with `einvoicing.tax_currency_not_entered` when a line
	// (but an exempt one) does not state it; one whose lines' VAT in AED does not sum to its VAT in AED
	// (IBT-111) is refused as `einvoicing.totals_inconsistent`. A valid tax credit note is entered the
	// same way as a supplier credit memo (T65e), naming as its reference the invoice whose number it cites
	// (IBT-025) by capture's rule: a posted invoice of the supplier in the company and the note's currency
	// is its `reference_invoice_id`; a number that is none enters it `on_hold`, its hold reason naming the
	// number, for a person to enter the reference; the memo keeps its reason (BTAE-03, `credit_reason`)
	// and each invoice it cites (`cited_invoices`: IBT-025 and, when stated, IBT-026, matched by number
	// and date); a tax credit note naming no invoice is held with
	// `einvoicing.credit_note_names_no_invoice` (a UAE tax credit note names the invoice it corrects,
	// IBG-03), nothing of it entered, rather than entered as correcting none, unless it is for a volume
	// discount (reason `VD`, IBR-055-AE), which is entered without a reference; one naming several
	// invoices (IBG-03 repeated) is entered as one credit memo citing them all, without a
	// `reference_invoice_id`, on hold naming any that is no posted invoice of the supplier (batch 88;
	// before it such a note was held with `einvoicing.credit_note_names_several_invoices`). A tax invoice
	// validated by a fetch before T65d, and a tax credit note validated before T65e, is entered by the
	// next one. When the fetch is done its Operation succeeds with the counts in its `result` (`recorded`,
	// `already_recorded`, `changed`: a message found with other bytes; `refused`: the documents this fetch
	// refused; `entered` and `held`: the documents this fetch entered and held; `waiting`: the connector's
	// documents left unprocessed, waiting for the company's setup) and its `resource` the list of the
	// documents it recorded, found changed, refused, entered or held
	// (`/v1/e-invoices?fetch_operation_id={id}`; a changed one names the fetch as its
	// `changed_fetch_operation_id`, one it processed, refused among them, also one an earlier fetch
	// recorded, as its `processed_fetch_operation_id`, and one entered or held as its
	// `entry_fetch_operation_id`); a message not recorded fails the Operation with
